--- !u!114 &1384706371
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1384706367}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 59293b856aaf48a4e8c51befc29d4e0c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  currentMode: 1
  labSaveKey: Lab1_InteractiveUnlocked
  btnModeExplore: {fileID: 738998378}
  btnModeInteractive: {fileID: 1008952730}
  rootExplore: {fileID: 1671187612}
  rootLearning: {fileID: 1780270161}
  rootInteractive: {fileID: 1477453251}
  uiPanelExploreLeft: {fileID: 1904170387}
  uiPanelExploreRight: {fileID: 1439921891}
  uiPanelLearning: {fileID: 2132723449347425948}
  uiPanelInteractive: {fileID: 26896922}
  uiModeSelection: {fileID: 0}
  explorePivot: {fileID: 1671187613}
  exploreDropdown: {fileID: 1688538729}
  exploreParts:
  - name: Anatomical Postion
    modelPart: {fileID: 940379544}
  - name: Saggittal plane
    modelPart: {fileID: 117590366}
  - name: Transverse plane
    modelPart: {fileID: 1375343533}
  - name: Coronal plane
    modelPart: {fileID: 390003403}
  sliderRotX: {fileID: 1897634917}
  sliderRotY: {fileID: 329609986}
  sliderRotZ: {fileID: 1135024295}
  sliderZoom: {fileID: 291417241}
  instructionText: {fileID: 1436199404625087210}
  btnNextStep: {fileID: 1271475074}
  btnPrevStep: {fileID: 1920110905}
  btnRestartLab: {fileID: 260491000}
  labAudioSource: {fileID: 544357010}
  enterExploreAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 96354d5de849ce144ab4d9125c14042f, type: 3}
  enterInteractiveAudio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 427616a12b40c6b41a21a276613ba9d5, type: 3}
  typeWriterSpeed: 0.05
  learningSteps:
  - name: Intro to Anatomical Position
    instruction: "Welcome to the Lab.\nObserve the Standard Anatomical Position:
      standing upright, feet together, arms at either side with palms facing forward.
      Observe the model to the right to see how this would look like in real life!\r\nThen
      afterwards, click on the \u2018next step\u2019 button to move onto the next
      part\r"
    visualRoot: {fileID: 201885007}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 0}
    requireInteraction: 0
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2388c30575dab1347b5fb358b34db1d0, type: 3}
  - name: ' Anatomical Directions '
    instruction: Understanding directional terms is essential for navigating the
      body. For example, 'Superior' means towards the head, while 'Inferior' means
      towards the feet. 'Medial' is closer to the midline, and 'Lateral' is further
      away. Observe the model to your right, compare it with the given diagram. Note
      how these terms map onto a real human body
    visualRoot: {fileID: 1748450927}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 0}
    requireInteraction: 0
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7f1bd7d66ad5dd541bd0bf089d6d6dda, type: 3}
  - name: 'The Sagittal Plane '
    instruction: This is the Sagittal Plane. It is a vertical plane that divides
      the body into Right and Left sections. Grab the plane to verify
    visualRoot: {fileID: 214245300}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 1255901708}
    requireInteraction: 1
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bca98238a0592734cb5300375763476c, type: 3}
  - name: 'The Transverse Plane '
    instruction: This is the Transverse Plane (or Axial). It runs horizontally, dividing
      the body into Superior (upper) and Inferior (lower) parts. Grab it to continue
    visualRoot: {fileID: 1003793616}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 505223256}
    requireInteraction: 1
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 59d4130b7cf4c9a479750a8fa5f92f00, type: 3}
  - name: 'The Coronal Plane '
    instruction: This is the Coronal Plane (or Frontal). It divides the body into
      Anterior (front) and Posterior (back) sections. Interact with the object.
    visualRoot: {fileID: 796929779}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 1193677680}
    requireInteraction: 1
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9262af99016ce32428d2789519cf8e3b, type: 3}
  - name: 'Areas of the Abdomen (Quadrants & Regions) '
    instruction: 'Clinicians divide the abdomen to accurately locate organs. The
      simple method uses four Quadrants, such as the Right Upper Quadrant. The precise
      method uses nine Regions, such as the central Umbilical region or the upper
      Epigastric region. Observe the highlighted abdominal grid to continue." '
    visualRoot: {fileID: 533804375}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 0}
    requireInteraction: 0
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 691b6f5dcf0876f4f9eecc1bc0d5df00, type: 3}
  - name: Outro_Finished
    instruction: Excellent work. You have identified all the major planes, directions,
      and regions of the body. You can now enter Explore and Interactive Modes to
      explore freely.
    visualRoot: {fileID: 201885007}
    interactionPart: {fileID: 0}
    requireInteraction: 0
    voiceClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bd2a9696b7c4d87489c5bb278d360f4d, type: 3}
